  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1050 AM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nWV imagery showing upper trough across eastern Utah/Arizona and\ncontinuing east. Weakening surface front just behind the trough\nalso pushing east. Moisture limited with this feature and mostly\nover northern New Mexico. Trough will sweep through the area\ntonight, with a slight chance of light showers over Otero and\nHudspeth Counties. Snow levels fall to as low as 6000 ft, so any\nshowers over the Sacs would be snow. Again limited moisture so\nrain/snow accumulations should remain quite low. \n\nTuesday and Wednesday...upper ridge builds in behind exiting\ntrough. Temperatures warm slightly as weak Monday cool front\nmoderates some. \n\nThursday and Friday...next Pacific trough moves toward the area.\nBlocking low over the central US/Great Lakes slows trough\nprogression down and strong jetlet back side of the trough allows\nfeature to dig south and close off low vicinity of southern Baja.\nFeature is able to tap into sub-tropical moisture but both\nGFS/ECMWF show low remaining well south of our area and not able\nto have much of an influence in our forecast. \n\nSaturday and Sunday...dry, zonal flow behind that exiting trough\nwill keep skies mostly clear with temperatures warming back up\nabove normal.",
